your fire, it's a person!

259
00:11:54,420 --> 00:11:55,340
Do something!

260
00:11:55,580 --> 00:11:57,286
He's escaping out the window!

261
00:11:57,440 --> 00:11:59,817
Great, now I have to shoot
at an invisible target?

262
00:11:59,900 --> 00:12:02,060
Special attack, gunpowder, star!

263
00:12:06,360 --> 00:12:07,920
But he must have escaped.

264
00:12:08,520 --> 00:12:11,500
Well, whoever it was, they heard it all.

265
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:13,257
Wait, who heard what?

266
00:12:13,340 --> 00:12:15,500
I still don't understand all this.

267
00:12:15,680 --> 00:12:17,268
You sure it wasn't my fart?

268
00:12:17,420 --> 00:12:19,400
He was in here the entire time.

269
00:12:20,060 --> 00:12:21,700
An invisible man.

270
00:12:22,520 --> 00:12:23,820
Well, this is no good.

271
00:12:24,100 --> 00:12:27,117
Thanks to this gigantic spider
web, we're dead in the water.

272
00:12:27,200 --> 00:12:28,657
Uh, no pun intended.

273
00:12:28,740 --> 00:12:31,037
Even if meeting that skeleton was a fluke,

274
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:34,157
the fact that the Thousand
Sunny and the Mini Mary both got

275
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:38,181
tangled up in this web in the exact
same spot is pretty damn fishy.

276
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:40,757
Somebody went to a hell
of a lot of trouble

277
00:12:40,840 --> 00:12:42,757
to make sure that when
we enter this place,

278
00:12:42,840 --> 00:12:45,487
it's through the front
gate and nowhere else.

279
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:47,630
Jeez,

280
00:12:47,713 --> 00:12:48,877
if they were going to
make it that obvious,

281
00:12:48,960 --> 00:12:51,317
they might as well have laid
out a welcome mat for us.

282
00:12:51,400 --> 00:12:53,717
Nero, what are you
mumbling about up there?

283
00:12:53,800 --> 00:12:54,957
You're going to miss all the fun.

284
00:12:55,040 --> 00:12:58,657
Are you seriously about to walk
into a trap that's so damn obvious?

285
00:12:58,740 --> 00:13:01,897
One even a headless zombie would
have the sense to run away from?

286
00:13:01,980 --> 00:13:03,039
Pretty much, yeah!

287
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:05,657
It's not like we have anything
better to do right now.

288
00:13:05,740 --> 00:13:06,570
It'll be fun!

289
00:13:06,800 --> 00:13:09,565
If you don't go, then
I'm taking your lunchbox.

290
00:13:15,100 --> 00:13:17,817
Why is there suddenly a
staircase leading down?

291
00:13:17,900 --> 00:13:19,017
It's the only way in.

292
00:13:19,100 --> 00:13:20,747
Let's just go with the plug.

293
00:13:22,380 --> 00:13:25,260
Hey, I wonder if these
skeletons can poop too.

294
00:13:33,460 --> 00:13:34,677
Check it out, everyone.

295
00:13:34,760 --> 00:13:35,590
It's Cerberus.

296
00:13:35,760 --> 00:13:38,217
We're literally on the
path to hell right now.

297
00:13:38,300 --> 00:13:39,977
Aw, I think it's kind of cute.

298
00:13:40,060 --> 00:13:40,897
Are they a threat?

299
00:13:40,980 --> 00:13:42,509
Because I'm feeling super.

300
00:13:42,860 --> 00:13:44,317
Three heads are overkill.

301
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:45,929
Blender with a teeth like.

302
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:55,005
Weird how they got all
riled up out of nowhere.

303
00:13:55,200 --> 00:13:56,030
Anyway.

304
00:13:56,280 --> 00:13:57,460
Uh-uh. Dips.

305
00:13:59,080 --> 00:14:01,020
I'm going to tame this bad boy.

306
00:14:01,740 --> 00:14:04,100
You idiot, you can't just tame it.

307
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:06,672
You do know it's not a regular dog, yeah?

308
00:14:07,220 --> 00:14:08,632
How different can it be?

309
00:14:08,840 --> 00:14:10,680
Come on, who's a good boy?

310
00:14:11,240 --> 00:14:12,070
Shake.

311
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:16,560
I assume we all saw this moment coming.

312
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:22,200
What big, strong teeth you have.

313
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:24,680
Now let go of Uncle Luffy's head.

314
00:14:24,880 --> 00:14:26,497
That's a good boy's.

315
00:14:26,580 --> 00:14:30,040
Easy does it, just like I said. No, shit!

316
00:14:33,580 --> 00:14:34,410
Roll over.

317
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:35,680
That just happened.

318
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:41,020
The poor thing's body
looks pretty beat up.

319
00:14:41,220 --> 00:14:43,537
I'm surprised it can still
walk around like that.

320
00:14:43,620 --> 00:14:47,037
I wonder what wise-ass put this thing
together, because whoever it was,

321
00:14:47,120 --> 00:14:50,577
they can't tell the difference
between a dog head and a fox head.

322
00:14:50,660 --> 00:14:53,017
If this is the first creature
we met on the island,

323
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:55,982
I can't wait to see what
other stuff we run into.

324
00:14:57,860 --> 00:14:59,957
Cerberus seems pretty down in the mouth.

325
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:00,897
Come on, Robin.

326
00:15:00,980 --> 00:15:01,810
Don't pity him.

327
00:15:01,893 --> 00:15:03,037
It just makes him feel worse.

328
00:15:03,120 --> 00:15:03,950
Leave him alone already.

329
00:15:04,033 --> 00:15:05,567
Can you hear me, Nami Sweet?

330
00:15:06,500 --> 00:15:07,330
Hello?

331
00:15:08,020 --> 00:15:10,420
Where are you, my feisty truffle?

332
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:14,374
I'm all turned around.

333
00:15:14,560 --> 00:15:16,097
It's like a maze full of creepy.

334
00:15:16,180 --> 00:15:17,040
Hey, wait up!

335
00:15:26,360 --> 00:15:31,007
A tree with some geezer's face is totally
getting drunk with a beat-up unicorn!

336
00:15:36,540 --> 00:15:37,900
Look what I got!

337
00:15:38,340 --> 00:15:39,940
Please, just let me go!

338
00:15:40,920 --> 00:15:42,060
They're so cool!

339
00:15:42,300 --> 00:15:43,677
How about you join my pirate crew?

340
00:15:43,760 --> 00:15:44,920
Overruled, dumbass!

341
00:15:55,920 --> 00:15:57,580
That was too close.

342
00:15:57,820 --> 00:15:59,517
You're there, right, Absalom?

343
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:00,600
I can never tell.

344
00:16:00,700 --> 00:16:01,917
What was all that ruckus?

345
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,706
Were you peeking in on
a bathing beauty again?

346
00:16:06,900 --> 00:16:09,600
I'm on the hunt for a bride, Hogback.

347
00:16:12,520 --> 00:16:13,640
The redhead.

348
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:15,620
I quite fancy her.

349
00:16:16,300 --> 00:16:18,340
I'll make her mine soon enough.

350
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:24,597
I hate to burst your bubble, but you
shouldn't go marrying the Golden Goose.

351
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:26,386
What's that supposed to mean?

352
00:16:27,260 --> 00:16:30,237
We have six guests with bounties
on their heads this time,

353
00:16:30,320 --> 00:16:31,897
including that girl you like.

354
00:16:31,980 --> 00:16:34,333
Her captain's worth 300 million berries.

355
00:16:34,660 --> 00:16:35,900
300 million?

356
00:16:37,460 --> 00:16:39,578
You don't seem very worried, Verona.

357
00:16:39,900 --> 00:16:43,297
If his bounty is that high, we can
only assume he's one tough customer.

358
00:16:43,380 --> 00:16:47,257
If you understand that, then you'll
know you have to go all out on this one.

359
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:49,281
And that means no chasing skirts.

360
00:16:49,600 --> 00:16:52,718
Looks like we'll have
ourselves a busy night tonight.

361
00:16:55,780 --> 00:16:57,497
Invisible men don't exist, Nami.

362
00:16:57,580 --> 00:16:58,410
End of discussion.

363
00:16:58,493 --> 00:17:00,217
I didn't imagine it, you ninny.

364
00:17:00,300 --> 00:17:03,617
When you came in there, you saw how it
was holding me off the ground, didn't you?

365
00:17:03,700 --> 00:17:04,530
Yeah, I saw.

366
00:17:04,613 --> 00:17:08,180
I mean, uh, sorry, Nami. Didn't
see a thing. Don't lie to me.

367
00:17:08,940 --> 00:17:10,057
Ah, trick question.

368
00:17:10,140 --> 00:17:10,970
That's no fair.

369
00:17:11,053 --> 00:17:13,937
As soon as I confess to seeing
you naked, I'm done for!

370
00:17:14,020 --> 00:17:15,697
You're gonna slap me into next week!

371
00:17:15,780 --> 00:17:16,610
Ah!

372
00:17:16,693 --> 00:17:18,537
I'm not trying to play mind games here!

373
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:19,677
The slapping can wait!

374
00:17:19,760 --> 00:17:20,760
See? I knew it!

375
00:17:20,900 --> 00:17:22,317
You wanna know what I think?

376
00:17:22,400 --> 00:17:25,677
Nothing I've seen on this island has
been real, including you being naked.

377
00:17:25,760 --> 00:17:27,819
The Invisible Man was just a draft.

378
00:17:27,940 --> 00:17:29,587
The ghosts were weird birds.

379
00:17:29,740 --> 00:17:32,357
And the zombies were just
some underground tribe.

380
00:17:32,440 --> 00:17:33,680
Are you nuts? Sure,

381
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:35,817
we ran into a fiddle-playing
skeleton with an

382
00:17:35,900 --> 00:17:38,257
afro who was brought back
to life by Devil Fruit,

383
00:17:38,340 --> 00:17:39,357
but he was the exception.

384
00:17:39,440 --> 00:17:42,197
No two devil fruits in
the world work the same.

385
00:17:42,280 --> 00:17:45,137
If his fruit brought him back
to life, then he's the only one.

386
00:17:45,220 --> 00:17:48,957
So zombies and ghosts and all the other
horrible stuff around here is impossible,

387
00:17:49,040 --> 00:17:49,922
right, Chopper?

388
00:17:50,760 --> 00:17:51,590
Huh?

389
00:17:51,860 --> 00:17:53,100
Come on, back me up.

390
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:54,520
The creatures we saw,

391
00:17:54,740 --> 00:17:57,937
there's no natural explanation
for them, so they can't be real.

392
00:17:58,020 --> 00:18:01,897
If you're looking at this from a medical
point of view, then you're correct, Usopp.

393
00:18:01,980 --> 00:18:04,921
There should be an explanation
for all this stuff.

394
00:18:05,280 --> 00:18:07,760
Then again, if Dr.

395
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:09,557
Hogback thought his work on the island was

396
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:12,464
important enough to leave
his whole life behind,

397
00:18:12,560 --> 00:18:16,795
maybe the natural order of things has
turned upside down on this island.

398
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:19,680
That is not what I wanted to hear.

399
00:18:19,800 --> 00:18:22,840
Maybe Hogback's not the
hero you think he is. Dr.

400
00:18:23,020 --> 00:18:25,637
Hogback is an amazing
man and a medical titan!

401
00:18:25,720 --> 00:18:27,057
I think he's incredible!

402
00:18:27,140 --> 00:18:28,777
How come you think the worst of him?

403
00:18:28,860 --> 00:18:30,797
We don't know if he's
friends with those zombies.

404
00:18:30,880 --> 00:18:32,017
You can't prove anything!

405
00:18:32,100 --> 00:18:32,930
Hey!

406
00:18:33,013 --> 00:18:34,380
All right, let's go ask Dr.

407
00:18:34,480 --> 00:18:35,833
Hogback what he thinks.

408
00:18:35,980 --> 00:18:36,980
How's that sound?

409
00:18:39,780 --> 00:18:41,380
That sounds horrible.

410
00:18:41,880 --> 00:18:44,233
I wish Luffy would hurry up and save us.

411
00:18:49,080 --> 00:18:53,397
I know I don't have anything to base it
on yet, but I don't trust that Hogback.

412
00:18:53,480 --> 00:18:54,833
He gives me the creeps.

413
00:19:04,340 --> 00:19:06,811
Isn't this the room we just ate dinner in?

414
00:19:07,440 --> 00:19:11,040
Yeah, so how come it's pitch
black in here? What the?

415
00:19:15,600 --> 00:19:18,660
Uh, Shandora, you around? Dr.

416
00:19:18,840 --> 00:19:20,660
Hogback, can you hear me?

417
00:19:20,960 --> 00:19:23,019
Yeah, we're done with the bathroom.

418
00:19:27,020 --> 00:19:31,020
I'm afraid the doctor and Shandora
have called it a day. Wait!

419
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:33,830
Hildon?

420
00:19:33,913 --> 00:19:34,743
Why, you little,

421
00:19:34,826 --> 00:19:37,917
what's the big idea ditching our carriage
in the middle of a scary graveyard?

422
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:39,420
I feel bad about that.

423
00:19:39,680 --> 00:19:42,297
Out of nowhere, I really
had to go to the bathroom.

424
00:19:42,380 --> 00:19:43,498
You know how it is.

425
00:19:43,660 --> 00:19:44,697
You're such a liar.

426
00:19:44,780 --> 00:19:45,677
Admit it, weirdo.

427
00:19:45,760 --> 00:19:47,097
You're in cahoots with those zombies.

428
00:19:47,180 --> 00:19:50,356
How could you say such awful
things about poor Hildon?

429
00:19:55,560 --> 00:19:57,560
But enough of that unpleasantness.

430
00:19:57,660 --> 00:19:59,757
If you'll follow me to the guest rooms...

431
00:19:59,840 --> 00:20:03,137
So if you don't turn us into Zombie
Chow at first, try, try again?

432
00:20:03,220 --> 00:20:06,632
I don't trust you any farther
than I can throw you, Pudgy.

433
00:20:06,720 --> 00:20:10,337
FYI, we're leaving here right now, and
there's nothing you can do about it.

434
00:20:10,420 --> 00:20:11,600
Huh? Wait a minute!

435
00:20:11,840 --> 00:20:13,597
Just let me trade things out with Dr.

436
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:14,510
Hogback!

437
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:18,300
Looks like you bungled it, Hildon.

438
00:20:20,100 --> 00:20:22,159
You don't have to be so mean to me.

439
00:20:22,360 --> 00:20:24,654
I'll take them up to their rooms, okay?

440
00:20:24,780 --> 00:20:26,920
I think it's a little late for that.

441
00:20:27,520 --> 00:20:30,461
These three have noticed
far too much around here.

442
00:20:30,920 --> 00:20:33,480
We can't risk them
telling anyone about us.

443
00:20:35,100 --> 00:20:36,820
I don't believe it!

444
00:20:37,780 --> 00:20:38,780
The painting!

445
00:20:39,280 --> 00:20:42,515
It's holding the conversation
with us like it's people!

446
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:45,940
You're so cute, I can
swallow you whole right now!

447
00:20:49,260 --> 00:20:50,560
Let go of him!

448
00:20:50,880 --> 00:20:52,437
The painting's trying to eat Chopper!

449
00:20:52,520 --> 00:20:53,814
I want to be a seller!

450
00:20:53,940 --> 00:20:55,437
Get your butt over here and help!

451
00:20:55,520 --> 00:20:56,800
I'm Oral Support!

452
00:21:04,160 --> 00:21:08,657
It is not the painting that you have to
worry about, but I, the Great Orchuk.

453
00:21:08,740 --> 00:21:12,837
You fools will never leave this room alive
again, so just get that out of your head.

454
00:21:12,920 --> 00:21:15,617
That mounted pig head on
the wall is talking too.

455
00:21:15,700 --> 00:21:17,000
And it threw a sword!

456
00:21:17,260 --> 00:21:21,907
I know you're busy, Nami, but there's a
pretty threatening taxidermy back here!

457
00:21:24,340 --> 00:21:25,280
Wait up.

458
00:21:25,540 --> 00:21:27,300
Is that a sword?

459
00:21:28,220 --> 00:21:31,400
Okay, who's the wise guy
who stabbed the bear skin?

460
00:21:35,780 --> 00:21:36,780
Nami was right!

461
00:21:36,900 --> 00:21:38,577
This mansion is wall-to-wall zombies!

462
00:21:38,660 --> 00:21:39,895
Even the decorations!

463
00:21:42,440 --> 00:21:43,580
What are you doing?

464
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:49,080
Here it comes!

465
00:21:50,260 --> 00:21:52,520
Eat this, you freaky undead frog!

466
00:21:54,980 --> 00:21:57,420
I can't believe you threw a candle at me!

467
00:21:57,620 --> 00:21:59,380
Seriously, who does that?

468
00:22:01,120 --> 00:22:02,420
We've gotta find him!

469
00:22:03,060 --> 00:22:04,717
The guy on the chandelier did it!

470
00:22:04,800 --> 00:22:07,137
Throw the candles in him,
see how much he likes it!

471
00:22:07,220 --> 00:22:11,397
Oh no you don't, because I know your
weakness, foul minions of the underworld!

472
00:22:11,480 --> 00:22:13,304
The power of Usopp compels you!

473
00:22:24,360 --> 00:22:26,200
Nami, Chopper, open the door!

474
00:22:26,440 --> 00:22:28,028
We need to get out of here!

475
00:22:28,220 --> 00:22:30,200
I don't care about Dr. Hogback!

476
00:22:30,380 --> 00:22:31,321
I want to leave!

477
00:22:31,880 --> 00:22:32,710
Open it!

478
00:22:32,793 --> 00:22:34,955
My heart can't take much more of this!

479
00:22:36,360 --> 00:22:38,060
What are you doing, Nami?

480
00:22:40,980 --> 00:22:42,237
You're kidding, right?

481
00:22:42,320 --> 00:22:43,260
No, I'm not!

482
00:22:43,500 --> 00:22:45,559
We're really trapped in here, Usof!

483
00:22:47,020 --> 00:22:50,220
How dare you set me on fire,
you dumb little Pierre!

484
00:22:52,060 --> 00:22:54,240
You're not getting away that easy!

485
00:23:01,380 --> 00:23:02,420
What now?!

486
00:23:09,500 --> 00:23:10,920
That was way too close!

487
00:23:11,120 --> 00:23:12,537
We gotta get to a different room!

488
00:23:12,620 --> 00:23:13,796
Anything beats this!

489
00:23:14,080 --> 00:23:15,420
Not so fast!

490
00:23:21,900 --> 00:23:22,940
No, no, no!

491
00:23:29,280 --> 00:23:30,633
This isn't the way out!

492
00:23:30,720 --> 00:23:32,014
It's just a fireplace!

493
00:23:36,320 --> 00:23:37,150
We're dead!

494
00:23:37,320 --> 00:23:39,640
There's nowhere else to run! Daddy!

495
00:23:46,060 --> 00:23:49,320
Where the heck are we?
Damn it! What happened?

496
00:23:49,640 --> 00:23:52,240
They disappeared all
of a sudden! Not quite.

497
00:23:52,420 --> 00:23:54,737
There's a secret passageway
behind the fireplace.

498
00:23:54,820 --> 00:23:56,837
If we don't catch them,
they're going to make it to Dr.

499
00:23:56,920 --> 00:23:58,273
Hogback's research lab.

500
00:24:04,100 --> 00:24:05,240
It's no good!

501
00:24:05,440 --> 00:24:08,087
They must be blocking
it from the other side!

502
00:24:11,640 --> 00:24:14,137
Run and run wherever
you like, little humans.

503
00:24:14,220 --> 00:24:18,396
You'll find that the mansion is full
of surprise zombies at every turn.

504
00:24:23,680 --> 00:24:25,060
This hallway is bad!

505
00:24:25,200 --> 00:24:27,082
Any place with paintings is bad!

506
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:30,471
There's gotta be a room in here somewhere!

507
00:24:30,640 --> 00:24:31,470
That's it!

508
00:24:49,560 --> 00:24:51,220
Oh, they're just photos.

509
00:24:52,280 --> 00:24:53,500
No zombies.

510
00:24:54,060 --> 00:24:55,120
Everything's fine.

511
00:24:55,920 --> 00:24:56,750
Hey, wait.

512
00:24:57,100 --> 00:24:58,688
It's that girl from before.

513
00:24:59,040 --> 00:25:01,440
The one who hates plates so much.

514
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:02,830
Shandora.

515
00:25:04,700 --> 00:25:05,530
It's weird.

516
00:25:05,800 --> 00:25:06,859
What is this room?

517
00:25:13,960 --> 00:25:16,937
Now that I get a better look,
she's really pretty, isn't she?

518
00:25:17,020 --> 00:25:19,317
She sure doesn't look
like a servant, though.

519
00:25:19,400 --> 00:25:20,230
But wait.

520
00:25:20,440 --> 00:25:23,205
You don't think this
place is her room, do you?

521
00:25:23,980 --> 00:25:25,333
That'd be a little odd.

522
00:25:25,760 --> 00:25:28,997
I mean, who would have so many photos
of themselves in their own room?

523
00:25:29,080 --> 00:25:30,857
What about all those
big stitches she's got?

524
00:25:30,940 --> 00:25:32,881
They aren't in any of the photos.

525
00:25:36,740 --> 00:25:37,660
You're right.

526
00:25:37,840 --> 00:25:39,117
And look at that smile.

527
00:25:39,200 --> 00:25:41,877
She's like a completely different
person than the one we met.

528
00:25:41,960 --> 00:25:44,617
Maybe these are old photos
and she had some accident.

529
00:25:44,700 --> 00:25:46,288
I mean, it's got to be her.

530
00:25:47,560 --> 00:25:49,100
Victoria Shandora. Huh?

531
00:25:50,120 --> 00:25:53,120
Evidently, she used to be
a really popular actress.

532
00:25:53,520 --> 00:25:54,440
Take a look.

533
00:25:54,780 --> 00:25:56,721
All these articles are about her.

534
00:25:57,360 --> 00:25:58,190
Huh?

535
00:25:58,360 --> 00:25:59,497
She was an actress?

536
00:25:59,580 --> 00:26:01,257
I thought they said she got into trouble

537
00:26:01,340 --> 00:26:03,277
for breaking a bunch
of plates or something.

538
00:26:03,360 --> 00:26:05,889
So you mean she wasn't
a servant after all?

539
00:26:06,160 --> 00:26:09,925
On the contrary, this says she
came from an aristocratic family.

540
00:26:10,860 --> 00:26:13,272
She had a successful career on the stage.

541
00:26:13,760 --> 00:26:16,500
And even as a child,
she had a lot of fans.

542
00:26:18,740 --> 00:26:19,620
What is it?

543
00:26:21,640 --> 00:26:23,960
These articles are old.

544
00:26:24,680 --> 00:26:28,780
Ten years ago, she fell from the
stage and died in an accident.

545
00:26:32,760 --> 00:26:34,080
That can't be right!

546
00:26:34,240 --> 00:26:35,397
We saw her ourselves!

547
00:26:35,480 --> 00:26:38,037
I mean, she is kind of creepy,
but she's definitely alive!

548
00:26:38,120 --> 00:26:38,950
He's right!

549
00:26:39,033 --> 00:26:41,765
So if what that article
says is true after all,

550
00:26:42,020 --> 00:26:44,017
she must have come back from the dead!

551
00:26:44,100 --> 00:26:45,512
There's no other answer!

552
00:26:48,320 --> 00:26:51,940
All those zombies we saw weren't
some kind of weird monsters!

553
00:26:52,300 --> 00:26:56,535
They were people and animals who had
died and been brought back to life!

554
00:27:08,320 --> 00:27:09,791
I don't like this at all.

555
00:27:10,160 --> 00:27:12,748
I don't even want to
think about it anymore.

556
00:27:13,420 --> 00:27:16,302
Let's just forget we ever
came here and run away.

557
00:27:17,700 --> 00:27:18,540
What now?

558
00:27:23,340 --> 00:27:24,260
Wait a sec.

559
00:27:24,420 --> 00:27:26,837
Is that what I think it is? It is.

560
00:27:26,920 --> 00:27:28,277
It's a treasure chest.

561
00:27:28,360 --> 00:27:29,860
Better already?

562
00:27:30,420 --> 00:27:32,197
Well, what are you waiting for, Usopp?

563
00:27:32,280 --> 00:27:33,500
Open it up, come on!

564
00:27:33,980 --> 00:27:35,020
All right!

565
00:27:38,120 --> 00:27:41,238
Sorry, suckers, but there's
no treasure in this room!

566
00:27:42,760 --> 00:27:43,860
It's a dragon!

567
00:27:49,420 --> 00:27:51,380
There you are!

568
00:27:53,140 --> 00:27:54,160
Hey, zombies!

569
00:27:59,040 --> 00:28:01,880
He said there was no
treasure in that room.

570
00:28:02,120 --> 00:28:04,767
They must be hiding
something somewhere else.

571
00:28:10,780 --> 00:28:11,610
Huh?

572
00:28:11,800 --> 00:28:12,980
It's the bodyguard.

573
00:28:13,300 --> 00:28:17,080
It seems some lost lambs have
wandered into the mansion.

574
00:28:17,380 --> 00:28:18,792
Oh, you're just in time.

575
00:28:19,180 --> 00:28:20,400
But never fear.

576
00:28:20,800 --> 00:28:22,620
I shall herd them up.

577
00:28:33,560 --> 00:28:36,677
For the last time, Luffy,
the skeleton was bad enough.

578
00:28:36,760 --> 00:28:39,217
We don't need trees and
unicorns on the crew.

579
00:28:39,300 --> 00:28:41,997
I mean, look, we've already
got a raccoon dog and a robot.

580
00:28:42,080 --> 00:28:42,910
That's messed up enough.

581
00:28:42,993 --> 00:28:44,857
Hey, how many times do I got to tell you?

582
00:28:44,940 --> 00:28:45,770
I'm not a robot.

583
00:28:45,853 --> 00:28:46,683
I'm a cyborg.

584
00:28:46,780 --> 00:28:47,617
All right, whatever.

585
00:28:47,700 --> 00:28:48,957
Either way, you're not human.

586
00:28:49,040 --> 00:28:50,137
In my heart, I'm a human.

587
00:28:50,220 --> 00:28:51,277
That's what matters.

588
00:28:51,360 --> 00:28:53,477
In your heart, you're a pervert, pal.

589
00:28:53,560 --> 00:28:55,760
Oh, then you understand after all.

590
00:28:55,880 --> 00:28:57,377
No, that was not a compliment.

591
00:28:57,460 --> 00:29:00,140
What kind of monsters are we gonna see?

592
00:29:00,440 --> 00:29:03,322
I hope they join the crew
and come along with me.

593
00:29:15,060 --> 00:29:17,037
There's something I
couldn't help but notice

594
00:29:17,120 --> 00:29:19,517
about that tree man and
the unicorn earlier.

595
00:29:19,600 --> 00:29:20,440
What's that?

596
00:29:21,720 --> 00:29:23,517
Just like our doggy friend here,

597
00:29:23,600 --> 00:29:26,117
all of the creatures in this
forest seem to have heavy injuries.

598
00:29:26,200 --> 00:29:31,340
Big stitches and numbers written on them
somewhere numbers, huh? That's true.

599
00:29:31,600 --> 00:29:34,077
I didn't put much thought into
it myself But are you saying

600
00:29:34,160 --> 00:29:37,037
these things are all working
for someone something like that?

601
00:29:37,120 --> 00:29:37,950
Yes?

602
00:29:38,460 --> 00:29:40,500
Hey guys, you hear those noises?

603
00:29:53,920 --> 00:29:54,960
That's awesome!

604
00:29:57,220 --> 00:29:58,050
Negative, negative, negative.

605
00:29:58,133 --> 00:30:00,657
Kind of annoying how they keep
saying negative over and over.

606
00:30:00,740 --> 00:30:02,617
I'm going to catch it
and keep it as a pick!

607
00:30:02,700 --> 00:30:04,617
Looks like it really is a ghost, huh?

608
00:30:04,700 --> 00:30:05,530
All right.

609
00:30:08,620 --> 00:30:09,580
Red Fire!

610
00:30:14,280 --> 00:30:15,220
Well, damn it.

611
00:30:15,420 --> 00:30:16,773
Guess that didn't work.

612
00:30:19,300 --> 00:30:20,720
I totally suck.

613
00:30:20,960 --> 00:30:23,257
Everything I did this week totally sucks.

614
00:30:23,340 --> 00:30:25,317
Everything I've ever done totally sucks.

615
00:30:25,400 --> 00:30:27,780
I might as well lie down and die.

616
00:30:28,880 --> 00:30:31,497
This should make me into a ceiling fan.

617
00:30:31,580 --> 00:30:33,637
So your attack didn't work!

618
00:30:33,720 --> 00:30:34,797
Don't be a baby!

619
00:30:34,880 --> 00:30:35,960
Okay.

620
00:30:40,520 --> 00:30:41,957
I wouldn't die.

621
00:30:42,040 --> 00:30:44,037
I'd be reincarnated as a clam.

622
00:30:44,120 --> 00:30:46,257
I can't cut it as a human.

623
00:30:46,340 --> 00:30:47,237
I'm useless.

624
00:30:47,320 --> 00:30:49,037
Just leave me here.

625
00:30:49,120 --> 00:30:50,397
Get over it already!

626
00:30:50,480 --> 00:30:52,304
What the hell's wrong with you?

627
00:30:53,700 --> 00:30:54,530
Negative.

628
00:30:54,900 --> 00:30:56,120
Negative, negative.

629
00:30:57,560 --> 00:31:00,537
It would appear that when the
ghosts pass through someone's body,

630
00:31:00,620 --> 00:31:01,657
they become depressed.

631
00:31:01,740 --> 00:31:03,477
And how does that make any sense?

632
00:31:03,560 --> 00:31:05,657
Those two are just straight-up pathetic.

633
00:31:05,740 --> 00:31:07,817
If they had even an ounce
of proper discipline,

634
00:31:07,900 --> 00:31:09,917
they wouldn't let themselves
fall to pieces over

635
00:31:10,000 --> 00:31:13,000
some measly little ghost
barely even touching them.

636
00:31:16,800 --> 00:31:18,740
I'm not even fit to be dog food.

637
00:31:19,020 --> 00:31:20,460
Okay, I get it.

638
00:31:20,600 --> 00:31:21,560
What a pain.

639
00:31:22,220 --> 00:31:25,357
Though it looks like Robin's
theory turned out to be spot on.

640
00:31:25,440 --> 00:31:30,157
None of our attacks can harm them.

641
00:31:30,240 --> 00:31:33,657
But if they pass through our
bodies, we'll be rendered helpless.

642
00:31:33,740 --> 00:31:36,697
They might prove troublesome
if we have to fight them.

643
00:31:36,780 --> 00:31:37,680
No kidding!

644
00:31:39,320 --> 00:31:40,837
What a strange island?

645
00:31:46,520 --> 00:31:48,814
Negative, negative, negative, negative.

646
00:31:51,020 --> 00:31:52,040
You know what?

647
00:31:52,180 --> 00:31:53,177
Screw you, ghost!

648
00:31:53,260 --> 00:31:54,777
I don't want to have you as a pet anymore!

649
00:31:54,860 --> 00:31:56,036
I want to crush you!

650
00:31:56,620 --> 00:31:58,757
Whatever their weak
point is, I'll find it.

651
00:31:58,840 --> 00:31:59,720
Just you wait!

652
00:32:01,800 --> 00:32:04,600
I should call you dog food. Shut up!

653
00:32:04,920 --> 00:32:07,697
The patchwork creatures with the
numbers on them may look frightening,

654
00:32:07,780 --> 00:32:09,157
but they seem easy enough to defeat.

655
00:32:09,240 --> 00:32:12,837
The ghosts, on the other hand,
seem to be exactly the opposite.

656
00:32:12,920 --> 00:32:15,391
There was one of them on the ship earlier.

657
00:32:15,720 --> 00:32:17,249
They show up, then vanish.

658
00:32:17,600 --> 00:32:19,776
Seems to me like they're watching us.

659
00:32:20,600 --> 00:32:24,306
If that's the case, the question
is, who's pulling the strings?

660
00:32:37,720 --> 00:32:39,320
Hey, check it out!

661
00:32:39,540 --> 00:32:40,893
It's a giant graveyard!

662
00:32:41,840 --> 00:32:42,670
Cool!

663
00:32:42,753 --> 00:32:45,640
Perfect place for a picnic,
don't you think? No way!

664
00:32:45,860 --> 00:32:47,978
This atmosphere will ruin the taste!

665
00:33:07,340 --> 00:33:10,300
Hey, don't put me back
on the ground, jackass!

666
00:33:14,500 --> 00:33:16,820
It's an old man with serious injuries.

667
00:33:17,260 --> 00:33:18,260
Are you nuts?

668
00:33:18,400 --> 00:33:19,280
It's a zombie!

669
00:33:20,120 --> 00:33:21,920
Don't make fun of me!

670
00:33:34,900 --> 00:33:37,660
Are zombies usually this... energetic?

671
00:33:38,320 --> 00:33:41,261
I'll show you how dangerous
zombies can really be!

672
00:33:44,280 --> 00:33:46,200
Oh, you guys want to fight, huh?

673
00:33:46,400 --> 00:33:49,224
Then I'll show you how
dangerous pirates can be!

674
00:34:01,640 --> 00:34:04,480
So, what are all you
guys doing out here, huh?

675
00:34:05,180 --> 00:34:11,240
Well, zombie stuff mostly, you know, being
buried, hanging out, rotting and stuff.

676
00:34:11,560 --> 00:34:13,437
Yeah, pretty much rotting and hanging out.

677
00:34:13,520 --> 00:34:14,660
Yep, same here.

678
00:34:16,440 --> 00:34:18,520
You're not lying to me, are you?

679
00:34:18,900 --> 00:34:21,037
No, really, that's the truth, we swear.

680
00:34:21,120 --> 00:34:22,617
Zombie stuff, that's all.

681
00:34:22,700 --> 00:34:23,940
I see.

682
00:34:24,240 --> 00:34:26,005
Then let me ask you something.

683
00:34:26,200 --> 00:34:29,700
Did a man with a long nose,
a woman with orange hair,

684
00:34:29,860 --> 00:34:33,566
and a reindeer that looks like
a raccoon dog come through here?

685
00:34:33,960 --> 00:34:36,480
Oh, yeah, right, right, right.

686
00:34:36,940 --> 00:34:39,937
We may have seen them, but
we're not supposed to...

687
00:34:40,020 --> 00:34:41,700
Sorry, we can't say.

688
00:34:42,180 --> 00:34:45,397
Oilers, oilers, oilers, oilers, oilers.

689
00:34:45,480 --> 00:34:46,400
Oh, I see.

690
00:34:46,620 --> 00:34:48,738
So you're not going to tell me, huh?

691
00:34:50,080 --> 00:34:51,777
I mean, yeah, we saw them.

692
00:34:51,860 --> 00:34:57,760
Those guys are part of my crew Listen up,
you didn't do anything to them, did you?

693
00:34:58,840 --> 00:35:00,480
Wait, they're on your crew?

694
00:35:00,840 --> 00:35:03,020
No, we didn't, right?

695
00:35:03,500 --> 00:35:06,140
Right, we did nothing at all.

696
00:35:06,940 --> 00:35:09,017
I want the truth right now!

697
00:35:09,100 --> 00:35:11,180
This guy did something.

698
00:35:11,860 --> 00:35:14,137
Hey, shut up, Tattletail!

699
00:35:14,220 --> 00:35:16,740
And anyway, you're the one that bit them.

700
00:35:17,980 --> 00:35:19,557
Actually, we all did.

701
00:35:19,640 --> 00:35:21,080
Idiots, shut up!

702
00:35:41,680 --> 00:35:43,720
I saw you fight those zombies.

703
00:35:44,780 --> 00:35:47,680
All of you have such
unbelievable strength.

704
00:35:49,640 --> 00:35:51,837
There's something I'd
like to talk to you about

705
00:35:51,920 --> 00:35:55,077
would you please listen old
man with serious Injuries

706
00:35:55,160 --> 00:35:59,797
idiot we told you they're
zombies oh actually he's

707
00:35:59,880 --> 00:36:02,837
right on the money that's
too Confusing can't you

708
00:36:02,920 --> 00:36:07,157
just be a zombie geez all
right so what did you want

709
00:36:07,240 --> 00:36:10,917
to tell us There's an evil
man who must be brought

710
00:36:11,000 --> 00:36:13,837
down and I think you
youngsters are strong enough

711
00:36:13,920 --> 00:36:16,940
to do it He's left a trail
of victims in his wake.

712
00:36:17,140 --> 00:36:19,611
If you defeat him, they'll all be rescued.

713
00:36:19,900 --> 00:36:23,488
If you'd help me get my shadow
back, I'd be ever so grateful.

714
00:36:24,580 --> 00:36:25,637
Let me take a look.

715
00:36:25,720 --> 00:36:26,920
It's true, see?

716
00:36:27,060 --> 00:36:28,417
He really doesn't have a shadow.

717
00:36:28,500 --> 00:36:30,220
He's just like Brooke.

718
00:36:30,700 --> 00:36:32,160
Well, damn, that sucks.

719
00:36:32,360 --> 00:36:34,540
So who did that to you? Is he here?

720
00:36:34,840 --> 00:36:36,311
Somewhere on this island?

721
00:36:39,600 --> 00:36:40,877
Mor... Moria.

722
00:36:40,960 --> 00:36:44,860
His name is Moria, and he's terrifying.

723
00:36:46,300 --> 00:36:47,130
Moria?

724
00:36:47,213 --> 00:36:48,257
You don't mean...

725
00:36:48,340 --> 00:36:51,820
Gecko Moria by any chance?

726
00:36:52,580 --> 00:36:53,580
That's right.

727
00:36:53,960 --> 00:36:55,240
Yes, that's him.

728
00:36:56,320 --> 00:36:58,020
Robin, do you know this guy?

729
00:36:58,300 --> 00:37:00,380
Yes, but only by name.

730
00:37:00,680 --> 00:37:05,445
And if I remember correctly, his former
bounty was even higher than yours, Luffy.

731
00:37:05,940 --> 00:37:07,260
Wait. Former?

732
00:37:07,520 --> 00:37:08,800
So that means...

733
00:37:09,640 --> 00:37:10,470
Yes.

734
00:37:10,553 --> 00:37:13,900
Gekkomoria is one of the
seven warlords of the sea.
